    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58134" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνηκός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνᾱκός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pale yellow, tawny</i>, of the goat, <i><span class="en">
				Thespis
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				7.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.32
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); so in oracular style, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				1034.23
			</span></i>; of the wolf, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				113.2
			</span></i>; cf. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνακός:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαρός, ἵππος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (Perh. cogn. with Skt.
			<i>kāñcanam</i> 'gold', OPruss.
			<i>cucan</i> 'brown', O<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>hunig</i> 'honey'.)</div>
